      "title": "In Canada",
      "body": "Say prices like this: 7,18 $ = sept dollars dix-huit (you do not need to say cents). 0,75 $ = soixante-quinze cents. 12 $ = douze dollars. For 1 200 $ say mille deux cents dollars. In Québec you may hear piastre for dollar and cenne for cent in casual talk. That is informal: you understand it, but you write dollar and cent."
